{"chapter": "algebraic", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04X4", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S \\to S'$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$S'$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:08eae98cf3075e3092ed363c012572b38e9b36b5cd43bd5f05aa0e522e8e5bd2", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a1a87a00094806379fb9dd7d9c9cde8307bfc710b0dce755b5f51c7ba7ce27bf", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn this section we briefly discuss what happens when we change base schemes.\nThe upshot is that given a morphism <MATH_0001> of base schemes, any algebraic\nstack over <MATH_0002> can be viewed as an algebraic stack over <MATH_0003>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:dc200f20e43f0f1323ed001b3902d420efb23fcc66d8e2251d31242ed699de6d", "unit_id": "tag:04X4:prose-0001"}
